IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sc-fi`

-- Family Independence (S.C. Code ch. 43-5) -- the applicant's and recipient's questions, worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the deposited text. Dollar figures for a grant or a payment standard are HYPOTHETICAL: the chapter does not set
-- them.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 43-5-1200: assets.
-- In work or training, one licensed driver, vehicles worth $8,000 and $3,000, other assets $1,500: the $8,000 vehicle is
-- left out; 3,000 + 1,500 = 4,500, over $2,500.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Are my assets within the limit` TRUE 1 (LIST 8000, 3000) 1500))
-- Two licensed drivers: both vehicles left out; 1,500.
#ASSERT `Are my assets within the limit` TRUE 2 (LIST 8000, 3000) 1500
-- Not in work or training: no vehicle is left out; 12,500.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Are my assets within the limit` FALSE 2 (LIST 8000, 3000) 1500))
-- Exactly $2,500 is within the limit ("The asset limit ... is two thousand five hundred dollars").
#ASSERT `Are my assets within the limit` FALSE 0 (LIST 2500) 0
#ASSERT `Are my assets within the limit` TRUE 1 (LIST 3000, 9000, 4000) 2500 EQUALS FALSE
-- One driver, three vehicles 3,000 / 9,000 / 4,000: the 9,000 one is left out; 3,000 + 4,000 + 2,500 = 9,500.
#ASSERT `countable assets` TRUE 1 (LIST 3000, 9000, 4000) 2500 EQUALS 9500

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 43-5-1205, 43-5-1210: income. Adults earn $800; a schoolchild earns $300 (left out); interest $450 ($400 left out);
-- other income $200: 800 + 50 + 200 = 1,050.
#ASSERT `How much of our income counts` 800 300 450 200 EQUALS 1050
-- Interest under $400 is left out entirely.
#ASSERT `How much of our income counts` 0 0 120 0 EQUALS 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 43-5-1170: time limits.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 10 30 `no exception` 0 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits: fewer than 24 months in the last 120 and fewer than 60 in my lifetime (s 43-5-1170)`
-- 24 months in the last 120: the next month would be the 25th.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 24 30 `no exception` 0 FALSE EQUALS `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`
-- 20 in the last 120 but 60 in a lifetime.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 20 60 `no exception` 0 FALSE EQUALS `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 20 59 `no exception` 0 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits: fewer than 24 months in the last 120 and fewer than 60 in my lifetime (s 43-5-1170)`
-- (1) permanently and totally disabled head of household.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 24 70 `the head of household is permanently and totally disabled` 0 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
-- (4) training: month 27 is within the 30; at 30 months only with the county director's permission.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 26 40 `I am in an approved training program that will not be completed by the twenty-fourth month` 0 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 30 40 `I am in an approved training program that will not be completed by the twenty-fourth month` 0 FALSE EQUALS `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))`
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 30 40 `I am in an approved training program that will not be completed by the twenty-fourth month` 0 TRUE EQUALS `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
-- (8) full compliance: 11 months of extension so far, so a 12th is allowed; at 12, only with permission.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 24 35 `I have fully complied with my agreement and no employment reasonably exists` 11 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 24 36 `I have fully complied with my agreement and no employment reasonably exists` 12 FALSE EQUALS `beyond the time limits unless the county director expressly permits (s 43-5-1170(4) or (8))`
-- (3) minor parent: up to 24 months after turning 18 or completing high school.
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 30 30 `the parent is a minor under 18 who has not completed high school` 23 FALSE EQUALS `within the time limits because an exception in s 43-5-1170 applies`
#ASSERT `Can we still get Family Independence under the time limits` 40 40 `the parent is a minor under 18 who has not completed high school` 24 FALSE EQUALS `beyond the time limits of s 43-5-1170`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The conditions of eligibility. A mother with a 4-year-old, resident, interview held, application complete, Social
-- Security numbers given, job search documented, in work or training, one driver, one car worth $6,000 and $800 in the
-- bank, no other issue, 10 months of receipt in the last 120, cooperating on child support.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my family meets the conditions the chapter states; whether we are needy, and the amount, depend on the department's income and payment standards`
-- Not a resident.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: we are not residents of South Carolina (s 43-5-70)`
-- Not in work or training: the car counts; 6,800 is over the limit.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: countable assets are over $2,500 (s 43-5-1200)`
-- Not cooperating on child support, no good cause: the child's aid becomes protective payments.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the child's aid is paid as protective payments, because I have not assigned support rights or cooperated on paternity and support (s 43-5-65(a)(2))`
-- An 18-year-old who is not a full-time student: no eligible child.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 18 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no child in the family is an eligible child`
-- An 18-year-old full-time high school student (s 43-5-95): the conditions are met.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 18 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my family meets the conditions the chapter states; whether we are needy, and the amount, depend on the department's income and payment standards`
-- A minor mother not living with her parents, no exception.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 2 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: a minor mother must live with her parent or guardian unless an exception applies (s 43-5-1220)`
-- Away from the State for 30 days or longer.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: I am or will be absent from the State for thirty days or longer (s 43-5-70)`
-- Beyond the time limits.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 24 40 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: beyond the time limits (s 43-5-1170)`
-- s 43-5-1190 applies and I do not submit to testing or treatment.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not eligible: random drug tests or an approved treatment program are required (s 43-5-1190)`
-- Job search not yet documented.
#ASSERT `Does my family meet the Family Independence conditions` 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 (LIST 6000) 800 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 10 10 `no exception` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not approved yet: the initial job search has not been documented (s 43-5-1120(B))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 43-5-148: benefits begin on the date of application if the conditions were met that day.
#ASSERT `From when do my benefits begin` (Date 14 9 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 9 2026)
#ASSERT `From when do my benefits begin` (Date 14 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 43-5-1175: receipt began 1 January 2025. A baby born 1 October 2025 (nine months on): the grant goes up. Born
-- 1 November 2025 (ten months on): no increase. Conceived by rape or incest: the cap does not apply.
#ASSERT `Will my grant go up for the new baby` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 10 2025) FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Will my grant go up for the new baby` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 11 2025) FALSE))
#ASSERT `Will my grant go up for the new baby` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 11 2025) TRUE

-- ss 43-5-1125(B), 43-5-1180: a 30-year-old parent of a 6-month-old: excused. A 22-year-old custodial parent without
-- high school, same baby: must take part. Youngest child 14 months: must. Six months pregnant, verified: excused.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I take part in employment and training` 6 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Must I take part in employment and training` 6 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I take part in employment and training` 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I take part in employment and training` 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I take part in employment and training` 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Dates.
-- A change learned of on 3 March 2026 must be reported by 13 March 2026 (ten calendar days).
#ASSERT `By when must I report the change` (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS Date 13 3 2026
-- Notice received 1 February 2026: review requested "not more than sixty days after": by 2 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for a review` (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS Date 2 4 2026
-- Conciliation from 1 March 2026: ends 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `When does my conciliation period end` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
-- Timely notice mailed 5 January 2026: the change cannot take effect before 15 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Earliest date the change can take effect` (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 15 1 2026

-- s 43-5-30(c)(2): HYPOTHETICAL grant of $300 for a family like mine; with no other income, the family may not go below
-- $270, so at most 30 a month is recovered of $500 owed. With $500 of earnings (income 800): 800 - 270 = 530, so the
-- whole 500.
#ASSERT `Most that can be recovered this month` 300 300 500 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `Most that can be recovered this month` 300 800 500 EQUALS 500

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The duties, in days.
-- A change reported on day 9: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `my duty to report a change` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `report the change to the department` 9)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Reported on day 12.
#TRACE `my duty to report a change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the recipient` DOES `report the change to the department` AT 12
-- expect: BREACH BY the recipient, "a change that may affect eligibility or the grant was not reported within ten calendar days; ..."

-- Agreeing to comply on day 20 of the conciliation period: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the conciliation period` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `agree to comply and resume the employment and training activities` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not by day 30.
#TRACE `the conciliation period` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31
-- expect: BREACH BY the recipient, "the thirty-day conciliation period ended without compliance ...: all AFDC benefits must be terminated; ..."

-- Requesting a review on day 59: fulfilled; not requesting one is no breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `my right to request a review` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `request a review of the decision` 59)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#TRACE `my right to request a review` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 61
-- expect: FULFILLED (a permission not used)

-- The department adjusts my grant on day 10 after receiving the information: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the department's duty to act on a change` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the department` `adjust the grant or redetermine eligibility` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
